abstract: >-
  Data and code accompanying the article "Circular economy pathways for
  steelmaking: resource footprints, fossil dependence, and value creation
  across metallurgical cycles" (Salashenko, Khaustova, Kyzym, Ilyash,
  Kotliarov, Shulga; submitted to Environmental Economics). The archive
  contains a domestic input-output base for Ukraine, India, the United
  States and Saudi Arabia (2015, 2019, 2021, 2022) aggregated from the OECD
  Inter-Country Input-Output tables (2025 edition) to 13 industries, a
  Jupyter notebook that computes all indicators of the study (input and
  output footprints, direct GVA shares, output and GVA multipliers,
  internal stability, external dependence and the classification of
  economic configurations), and the resulting tables and figures.
keywords:
  - circular economy
  - iron and steel industry
  - input-output analysis
  - OECD ICIO
  - gross value added multiplier
  - R-principles
